  "answer": "**Not all checks pass.** The build passed, but the unit stage failed, so the component stage was skipped. The run halted early (run `20261021T070604Z-99ba37`).\n\n| Stage | Result |\n|---|---|\n| build (`make build`) | passed |\n| unit (`make unit`) | **failed**, exit code 2 |\n| component (`make component`) | skipped |\n\n**Unit tests:** 272 total, 233 passed, 39 failed. That count comes from the log's own summary. A grep of the log shows each failing test listed twice, which fits the two target frameworks (net9.0 and net10.0).\n\n**All 39 failures have one cause.** They throw `System.ArgumentException`, for example `Unknown semantic matcher 'isuuid' for field 'id'`. The other names in the same error are `isisodatetime`, `isisodate`, `isemail`, `isnull`, `isnotnull`, `isempty`, `isnotempty`, `greaterthan`, `lessthan`, `haslength` and `isdomainid` (a custom matcher). The exception is thrown from `SemanticMatcher.Apply` in `src/ConfIT/Matching/SemanticMatcher.cs`.\n\nThe spec parser lowercases matcher names (`ToLowerInvariant()` at lines 85 and 91). The `BuiltIns` dictionary at lines 8\u201322 uses camelCase keys such as `\"isUuid\"` and has no case-insensitive comparer. So the lowercased name never matches. I didn't confirm that the custom matchers are looked up the same way.\n\n**Failing tests by group:**\n- `SemanticMatcherTests`: about 32 `Apply_*` tests. These cover every built-in matcher (isUuid, isIsoDate, isIsoDateTime, isEmail, isNull/isNotNull, isEmpty/isNotEmpty, greaterThan, lessThan, hasLength), the custom-matcher test (`Apply_CustomMatcherName_DelegatesToCustomFunc`), `Apply_NullExpected_DoesNotThrow` and `Apply_NestedFieldPath_PassesForValidValue`. `Apply_FieldAbsentFromResponse_ThrowsInvalidOperationException` also fails, because the unknown-matcher error is thrown before the expected exception.\n- `ResultMatcherTests`: 5 tests that use semantic matchers.\n  - `MatchResponseBody_AllThreeMatcherTypes_EachApplied`\n  - `MatchResponseBody_SemanticMatcherFails_ReturnedDescriptionNamesField`\n  - `MatchResponseBody_SemanticMatcherValid_PassesAndRemovesField`\n  - `MatchResponseBody_CustomMatcher_PassesForValidValue`\n  - `MatchResponseBody_NullExpectedWithSemanticMatcher_DoesNotThrow`\n\nI didn't modify any files. The `cd` I ran into the run directory only affects the shell's working directory.",
